      Announcing the Release of Version 1.08 of V -
      The Easiest Way to Write C++ GUI Applications

                     April 18, 1996

Version 1.08 of the V C++ GUI Framework was released
on April 18, 1996. With this release, the versions
for X and Windows are now in sync. Of major significance
is the release of WIN32 support for NT and Win95.

Version 1.08 also includes several new features, including
a memory canvas and a toggle button control.

*** WHAT IS V?

V is a portable C++ GUI Framework intended to develop a wide
variety of applications on different graphical interface
platforms. While it is probably not suitable for developing
state-of-the art commercial applications with all the latest
interface components, it is very complete and suitable for a
large majority of custom GUI applications. Applications developed
using V will have the look and feel of the native platform, yet
will be portable across platforms.

Most standard GUI objects are supported by V, including windows
with menus, status bars, tool bars, and a drawing canvas; modal
and modeless dialogs with the most common controls (buttons,
lists, labels, text entry, check and radio buttons, etc.); and
portable printing support.


*** WHAT V USERS ARE SAYING

