The first version of the Linux Graphics mini-Howto is now available from
http://www.csn.net/~mjhammel/linux-graphics-howto.html.  Greg Hankins 
reported he will be adding this document (if he hasn't already) to 
the Linux Documentation Project (LDP) page at 
http://www.cc.gatech.edu/linux/ldp/linux.html.

This document describes the tools available for use on Linux for viewing,
creating, and manipulating graphical images as well as tools for converting
between various image formats.  There is also a short section on what tools
to use for creating Web pages and some issues with which HTML authors should be
concerned when dealing with graphics images in their documents.  Issues
regarding both static image tools and animation tools are discussed.  

There are currently no sections regarding Java or VRML, however I would very 
much like to hear from persons who've done work in these areas on Linux so
that I may add these sections in later releases.

This will be a constantly evolving document.  There are many tools which
are only lightly covered because I have little informtion on them currently.
I'm very open to comments on this document so if you find mistakes,
omissions or other errata please feel free to contact me at
mjhammel@csn.net.

