Well, the first bug-fix release of pnews, pnews-0.11 is ready.

I still consider it alpha, but it should work on more platforms now.

pnews (not Pnews!) is a simple system that uses suck to pull news from a
remote NNTP server and put it into a local spool where it may be read with
any newsreader that is capable of dealing with a local news spool (I have
plans to add a tiny NNTP server for those newsreaders that are
spool-ignorant, but that's a ways down the road).

pnews will also spool outgoing messages to send later when a SLIP or PPP
connection is made.

pnews should work with almost any NNTP server that can be used with a
newsreader. suck (the program that pnews uses to get news) takes pains to
look like a newsreader when it connects.

You will have to obtain suck to use pnews, I included directions to get it
and a list of sites.

pnews was written to provide a tiny alternative to cnews or INN. Unlike
cnews or INN, pnews is unsuitable for a full newsfeed. It is intended for
one or two users reading maybe 10-20 groups. I'm sure it can handle more
than that, but even 1/10 of a full feed would break it badly. Really badly.
It's a personal news system.

pnews may be downloaded from:

http://www.holli.com/~jbuchana/computer.html

Good luck, and thanks to all the people (especially Richard VanHouten and
Gavin Treadgold) who've tried pnews and made suggestions!


