-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

This is the ALPHA release of a kernel patch that improves
performance on NexGen CPUs in kernels 1.3.82 and beyond.  
(With a minor change it will work in earlier kernels as well.)

Some background: Kernels configured for CPU "386" work fine 
on NexGen Nx586 systems.  However, one of the differences 
introduced by configuring for "486" or better CPUs is more
efficient handling of the on-chip cache of virtual memory 
page table entries, to reduce the number of page traps after 
a memory allocation/mapping operation.  This patch extends
those benefits to Nx586 systems.

What and how: The patch modifies the configuration scripts,
the CPU-type detection code, and the page-table handling code.
To use it, apply the patch; run "make config" and choose a
CPU type "Nx586"; then "make clean" etc.

The patch can be found at:

  http://www.cantrip.org/ncm.html

If you have a NexGen system, be sure to get on the mailing list 
mentioned there. (Thanks to Russ Nelson, http://www.crynwr.com/~nelson/
for setting up the mail reflector.)

Nathan Myers
ncm@cantrip.org  http://www.cantrip.org/


