The "new and improved?" version of RCS described below is based on RCS 5.7 - 
which means that it probably should have been numbered 5.7.1.1.  :-)
Don't get terribly attached to the 6.0, because neither the version number 
or the "enhancements" have been endorsed by the official RCS maintainer.  I'm
still waiting to hear from Paul (I sent him a description of the changes last
fall, but got no response.)  The last thing I want to do is create confusion
over a version number when the real 6.0 eventually comes out.
Some people might disagree with putting a thread mechanism at the RCS level
(no intention of angering all you CVS fans out there).  Please check out the
implementation description in rcs60thr.txt before writing it off - the
mechanism is useful for controlling the checkout of individual files as well
as groups of files.  If there are requests for more/improved thread features,
let me know.  (At some point the simple wildcard matching may be replaced by
regex symbol matching - although this might be dangerously ambiguous.)

- -Terry Tompkins

