My new news software, pnews (not Pnews!) is ready for alpha.

A few months ago, I decided that I wanted to read news off-line under Linux.
I got suck from sunsite, and it got the news from my NNTP server well, but
didn't spool it.

The documentation suggested cnews or INN for this.

I looked into it, but either one seemed overkill for a tiny personal site,
so I decided to write my own smaller, simpler software to spool incoming and
outgoing news.

I called it pnews despite the possibility for confusion with Pnews, the
posting program (which will work with pnews).

It is now ready for alpha testing by any brave souls who are interested.

The alpha version is available as tarred, gzipped C source code at:

http://www.holli.com/~jbuchana/computer.html

(There's a few perl scripts I get a lot of use from there too)

Feel free to get a copy and give it a try. Please let me know about your
likes, dislikes, bugs and wish-list. Any "you just reinvented the wheel"
flames will be ignored. I justified myself as far as I'm going to in the
fourth paragraph.

Thanks!


