Hi everybody!

XBanner 0.9a is a minor release of XBanner, that fixes a few minor bugs.

I have just uploaded XBanner 0.9a to the Incoming directory on sunsite. It
should be moved soon to /pub/Linux/X11/xutils. This release fixes some minor
bugs, improves performance for to of the effects, and some misc. clean-up
of the code. See the file docs/Changes in the distribution.

	Amit

- ----------------- Annoouncement of XBanner 0.9 --------------------------
Hello All!

I am very happy to announce that XBanner 0.9 is now available. This version
contains several very important enhancements:
1. Performance improvements - EVEN MORE! Effects are now 40% faster than
   in v0.05 (which was the previous version).
2. Option to underline your text. Also possible to have XBanner render the
   effects on the underline if you like.
3. X-Resources! XBanner now uses an app-defaults file with real X resources.
   Root's .Xdefaults and the Display's loaded resources are taken as options.
4. Complete command-line interface (well, almost anything can be done from
   command-line).

What Is It?
- -----------
Do you run XDM? Does your system load the X-Window system and then asks for
your username/password? If this is the case XBanner can make that login
screen look much much nicer.

XBanner simpy takes the text you tell it to, and draws it onto the screen
in a font of your choice. It renders an effect that you can choose for you
and some of these effects can look awsome.

I have uploaded it to sunsite.unc.edu in the /pub/Linux/Incoming directory,
and it should soon be moved to /pub/Linux/X11/xutils.

Here's the LSM:

Begin3
Title:		XBanner          
Version:        0.9
Entered-date:   7-Apr-1996
Description:    This program draws a text line on the X root window with
		some nice effects. It is meant to be run by XDM's Xsetup_0
		script, to give a nice XDM's login box a nice touch.
Keywords:       X, X-Windows, XDM, X11, banner
Author:         amitm@doronx.iso.dec.com (Amit Margalit)
Maintained-by:  amitm@doronx.iso.dec.com (Amit Margalit)
Primary-site:   sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/X11/xutils
		27Kb XBanner0.9.tgz
		584  XBanner0.9.lsm
Platform:       X11R5, gcc, xdm
Copying-policy: GPL
End

What's new in 0.9? (excerpt from the Changes file)
- ---------------------------------------------------
v0.9	- Retouched some of the code that selects the relevant portion
	  of the screen so the XImage routines don't take too long.
	  I hope I got it right this time ;-)
	- Removed some extraneous storing of zeros into zero-filled arrays
	  (I got them from calloc() and still stored 0's in them).
	- Added placement type "CenteredOnY". This centers the text line
	  on a given line. The Y value comes from Xbanner.Y and the X is
	  simply centered on that line (first step towards an idea by
	  Doug Ford).
	- Fade and Backlight are almost the same so I merged them to 1 func.
	- Cleaned the code a bit more
	- *** Now using real X resources. Some changes were necessary to
	  the names of the options. These are documented in the file
	  Resources.doc (along with a comrehensive list of all resources).
	- The above means a whole set of command line option. Try xbanner -h!
	- For using resources properly in X11R4 (that's only for my Ultrix
	  at work, I know, but...) there is a #define in xb_config.h
	- Error messages now carry a nice "XBanner:" prefix so you'll know.
	- xb_config.h option "RW_COLORS" has been removed. We now actually
	  check for the visual type to see if it can use R/W colors.
	- Improved the performance of all new effects at a very low cost
	  in memory consumption. Should be real good now.
	- Some more cleaning of the code from global variables
	- We now make sure that we need the FadeFrom/FadeTo colors before
	  allocation.
	- Reworked the placement code completely. I hope there will be no
	  more problems with it now.
	- New option: Undelined text. The resource is "XBanner.underlined",
	  you can select the thickness "XBanner.underlineThickness" and the
	  color "XBanner.underlineColor". Special color name "fgc" will use
	  the FG color, which will render some of the effects on the
	  underline as well as the text.

>> We jumped to 0.9 here because a first major release is pretty close now!

*** Important! I am looking for beta testers. This program has reached a
    stage where it is important that I get feedback about bugs lurking
    in the code. I'd really appreciate any comments.

						Amit Margalit
						amitm@doronx.iso.dec.com


