XmToolbar 1.1:

I have uploaded a new version of XmToolbar to sunsite.unc.edu.
The files are now in "/pub/Linux/Incoming" and should soon be moved
to "/pub/Linux/X11/xutils/toolbars/xmtoolbar-source-1.1.tar.gz"

The files can also be downloaded at
        "http://www.atnet.at/club/spiff",
the official homepage for XmToolbar.

What is it??
- ------------
XmToolbar is an application launcher for Linux and X11 (requires
Motif 2.0 or 1.2.4). It was developed on Linux, but should work
with other Unix versions as well (like BSD or Solaris)

What can it do that a console can not ?
- ---------------------------------------
Nothing, but it looks nice ;)

Thanks to Bob Mallozzi there are two new features:
    * start instances of xmtoolbar with various config files
    * set the position for xmtoolbar at startup
I added (just to do something for a new release):
    * descriptions for every button
and made a new version out of it (great - huh!!)

Of course the old features are still there:
    * configuration via the application with a preference dialog
      and popups (I HATE to edit config files)
    * group buttons for applications of the same type
    * quick infos (tool-tips) like in Windows
    * shrink the toolbar at one mouse click
    * color pixmaps
    * add and delete buttons as you wish while running xmtoolbar
      (no restart to see changes)

So, get a better Unix life and get it !!

If you have suggestions or just want to flame (but don't be upset if
I flame back :) ), write to:
        spiff@calvin.priv.at

bye,
        tom.



