There were no announcements for about a week during Easter.  Sorry.

My incoming box is empty now.  Sorry about the avalanche.

I'd had trouble with my old hard disk, and it finally died.  At about
the same time, I noticed that my floppy drive and tape didn't work very
well together.  So I spent several days debugging and reinstalling my 
system.  I had hoped to do a few other things, but such is life.

Things are working again.  I haven't even lost any data, except for
a few megabytes of icons, which I thought were on a different partition
(there was only a symlink).  Oh well, they can easily be downloaded again.

For those interested, I'm using Debian (the development version).  This
is not an endorsement, but I happen to prefer it over Red Hat.  Besides,
since Linus uses Red Hat, someone has try out the other distributions. :-)

I use PPP over a 14.4 kbps modem to download mail, mirror a few ftp sites, 
and to connect to the university via ssh or telnet.  I don't appreciate
getting huge amounts of mail, and in the past week or so, several people
have sent me binaries intended for comp.os.linux.announce.  Please don't
do that, I won't post them anyway.



