April 10, 1996

                         Snapix SEL Press Release


SNAPIX SEL for LINUX
- --------------------
SNAPIX Special Edition for LINUX (SEL) is now available free via the Internet 
for personal use. 

SNAPIX is an interface and application generator which allows you to use X11 
and Motif libraries under Unix with ease. 

Creating superb quality graphical applications is now within the reach of any 
developer - with SNAPIX there is no need to consult the X11 and Motif 
documentation, nor to know about callback routines or widget trees. 

SNAPIX significantly reduces the length of the development cycle thanks to its 
easy to use, graphics editor which is synchronised with the program text editor.

SNAPIX provides a true object oriented, event-driven language (inheritance, 
polymorphism, instantiation, messages, etc.) 

Within only a few hours of getting to know SNAPIX you will be able to start 
designing your first graphical applications. 

SNAPIX SEL is supplied complete with statically linked Motif libraries 
(Metrolink), so no royalties are due to OSF or Metrolink. 

Commercial versions of SNAPIX are available for SCO, ISC, SVR4 (Unixware), Linux,
Lynx Os, Solaris (X86 and Sparc), AIX, HPUX, etc. - however, in these cases, 
you must have a full commercial Motif license. 

SNAPIX - a stable product 
- -------------------------
The first version of SNAPIX based on the syntax still in use today was 
delivered in February 1990 (FCS). Since then SNAPIX has been greatly enhanced 
with new properties, functions and objects and ever-improving performances. 
SNAPIX is a mature, robust product, well able to meet the requirements needed 
to build fast, friendly, reliable applications. 

Applications 
- ------------
Our clients use SNAPIX for all kinds of applications from re-usable prototypes 
to commercial products with tens of thousands of lines of code in a wide range 
of professional situations.

