We continue to hear complaints that people cannot find Linux Journal on
newsstands.  We would like to enlist your help in solving the problem.
One very important reason to help is that many people find out about Linux
or get their first taste that there is a real Linux community by seeing
the magazine on newsstands.

The two parts of the problem are newsstands that sell out and that many
newsstands don't know there is any demand.  The "sold out" problem is
something that we at LJ and our newsstand distributors need to work on but
getting LJ in more newsstands is where we need your help.

First, ask at the newsstand if they carry LJ.  If they say no, suggest
they should.  Telling someone you want to buy something from them is the
best way to get them interested.  You can tell them to call us directly
(206-782-7733) about distribution information or contact either of our
distributors: Ingram or IPD.

Then, tell us what you did.  If you e-mail the contact information of the
distributor to dist@ssc.com we will send them a sample magazine and
distribution information.  And maybe LJ will replace Mac World if we do
our job right. :-)

