		    POSTIT - An NNTP client for posting
		    ===================================

			      Version 0.5
		       Written by Egil Kvaleberg
				    
				 ------

Postit is an NNTP client that is capable of submitting articles generated
in a local news spool to the remote NNTP using the POST command.

Together with e.g. Slurp, it will provide the NNTP capabilities required for
small news spools on installations with NNTP access only through limited
ISP accounts with dialup SLIP/PPP connection.

The main improvements for the 0.5 version are:

- - Can maintain a log of successfully posted articles.

- - Can collect all posted articles in a folder.

- - Source code extensively rewritten, removing dependence on other code.

- - Improved batch file locking.

- - Compatible with Cnews and INN.

As always:

- - Error recovery. In the event of an error occurring while articles are
  being posted, the failed articles are maintained in the spool file
  pending retries.

- - Logging to syslog of the number of successfully posted, missing and
  duplicate articles at the end of a session plus, if required, the
  transfer speed of the article posting stage.

Postit was written in C under Linux, and should be quite portable.

