Version 0.4 of Xmemuse has been released.

You can find it in the sunsite Incoming directory but should be at the
right place soon (sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/X11/xutils/status).

Xmemuse shows the memory layout (buffers, cached, free, used, swapped)
in a display (like xload). It uses /proc/meminfo to obtain this
information. Somewhere around linux 1.3.50 the format of /proc/meminfo
changed, this release should handle both corretly.
In the previous versions of Xmemuse, shared memory was
displayed as part of the used memory. But since the shared memory
number says nothing about memory use (if I am correct it only says how
much memory extra would be used if there was no memory shared), so now
a seperate line for it is drawn.

Check it out!

