I've written a spiffy little filter and script which will download a html 
file, and then recursively chase and download each of the links and 
inline images it refers to.  The resulting source tree is suitable for 
running off a local httpd - all of the absolute links are changed to refer 
to files relative to the current html file.

Snag-o-rama requires access to the lynx text-based browser, to do the 
actual downloading of files over a http connection.

Here's the lsm entry:

Begin3
Title: snag-o-rama-1.2       
Version: 1.2
Entered-date: 4/21/96  
Description: Uses lynx to download an entire html source tree from a remote 
	     URL; recursively chases image and hypertext links.
Keywords: www http html lynx
