Xzoom is a small program that like xmag magnifies an area of the
X11 display.
Xzoom allows change of magnification factor (X and Y magnification
can be controled separately). Rotate the displayed image by a multiple of
90 degrees or mirror the image about the X or axes.
Xzoom repeats 'zooming' to the same area and on my system (486DX66
+CLGD5428) it is fast enough to display small aninations (ie., run
xanim in one window and see the zoomed animation in another).
Parameters can be changed at any time by hiting keyboard keys
when the input focus is on the xzoom window. The xzoom window
can be resized at any time and if it is iconified it will stop
consuming CPU (well... I hope).

Currently it supports only 8-bit depth displays. It was tested
only under Linux 1.3.x and XSVGA 3.1.2.

Enjoy it.

Itai Nahshon


