   This is to announce a new release of my port of Linux to the Motorola
MVME166 and MVME167 boards.  A single tar file can be found in

	680x0/vme/linux166-pl3c.tar

on your local linux-68k archive site (eg. ftp.uni-erlangen.de, mirrored
onto tsx-11 etc).  The port is based on the Atari/Amiga port of Linux,
release 1.2.13pl3.

The MVME166 and 167 boards are VME cards with 68040, NCR 53C710 SCSI,
ethernet, four serial ports (Cirrus Logic CD2401), timers, etc.

The major improvement in this release is that the SCSI driver is now
based on Drew Eckhardts release 16 driver for the NCR53C810, and
supports multiple disks, disconnect/reselect, and synchronous working.
Ethernet support for these cards is not yet available.

The tar file contains a full source tree, a pre-compiled kernel for use
with a ram disk, and instructions.  

Any reports of success or failure with this port will be gratefully
received.

Vaughn Skinner <vaughn@solid.net> has successfully ported my previous
release to the MVME162 board.

Many thanks to the Atari and Amiga guys and to Drew for the code I based my
port on, and, of course, to everyone involved in Linux itself.  Thanks also
to those who provided feedback on the previous release.

Richard Hirst	richard@sleepie.demon.co.uk


