-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

The 2.0 release of MetaCard Corporation's award-winning GUI
application and hypermedia environment for UNIX/X11 workstations is
now available.  GUI application developers currently using low-powered
tools that rely on C or C++ and Xt/Motif can dramatically increase
their productivity with MetaCard, and developers using Tcl/Tk, the
COSE Desktop KornShell, or other high-level tools can now deliver
high-performance applications without having to rewrite the
computation-intensive routines in C.

MetaCard is also a complete multimedia authoring tool and hypertext
documentation tool, so you can use it not only to develop GUI
applications, but also to produce on-line documentation and
Computer-Based Training (CBT) for them.  MetaCard truly has a unique
combination of features:

High productivity:
  MetaCard's built in layout and image editing tools,
  syntax-highlighting script editor, and GUI script debugger make
  application development, from prototype to release, faster and
  easier than ever before.

High capability:
  MetaCard has built-in support for object-oriented (vector) and
  bitmap (GIF, JPEG, XPM, XWD, XBM, BMP, PBM) graphics.  The MetaCard
  text field control supports multifont, multicolor text with
  subscript-superscript and hypertext links. 

High-level language:
  MetaTalk now supports associative arrays, regular expression pattern
  matching, call-by-reference arguments, and custom object properties
  with setprop and getprop "triggers" and persistence support OO
  programming and database development techniques.

High performance:
  The MetaTalk script "virtual compiler" has performance comparable to
  Perl and Java, and up to 30 times better performance than Tcl/Tk 
  and the COSE Desktop KornShell, without being plagued by the
  syntactic complexity of these other languages.

MetaCard is a commercial product ($995) available on 13 UNIX/X11
platforms, and soon on Windows 95/NT.  Run-times are freely available
from our FTP and WWW sites, and can be easily and securely used as
helper applications with WWW browsers.

For more information on MetaCard including a detailed comparison of it
with Tcl/Tk and dtksh (with benchmarks), see http://www.metacard.com
or download a free save-disabled evaluation copy of MetaCard with
anonymous FTP from ftp://ftp.metacard.com/MetaCard.  Downloading and
installation is very easy and non-intrusive (no forms to fill out, no
need for root access to install, and the installed distribution is
under 5 MB on all platforms which is compressed to less than half that
size for download).  You can also get MetaCard via email from
support@metacard.com (please specify the platform and OS you'll be
using it on).

