   Free for academic use,  30 day evaluation period, licence fee of
   R2500  (about 400 Pounds Sterling).

Here's the announcement:

                                                 3 April 1996
                                                 Thawte Consulting
                                                 South Africa


For Immediate Release
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

ANNOUNCING:  Sioux: High-performance secure web server
Platform:    All major UNIX variants



Thawte Consulting today announce the availability of the gold release
of their high-performance secure web server, Sioux.

The server is currently available for LinuxELF, with ports to
Solaris 2.5, Irix, HPUX, AIX and other major UNIX's in progress.
Solaris 2.5 will be available on Thurday 4 April.
It can be found at:

   ftp://ftp.inect.co.za/pub/products/sioux/
   ftp://ftp.thawte.com/pub/products/sioux/

Sioux offers some unique features for those clients who need tight
certificate-based access control. It supports full digital encryption
worldwide, and has been optimised for maximum performance in an
Intranet as well as Internet environment.

"We wanted to create a web server which would set the pace in terms
of client authentication and certificate management" said Mark
Shuttleworth,  Managing Director of Thawte Consulting. "Sioux
meets that expectation easily. It provides the international market
with a powerful platform for secure online commerce."

Some of the leading features of Sioux are:

  - sophisticated client certificate management

    Sioux allows you to specify exactly who can access parts of
    your web server based on their digital certificate. For example,
    you can say "admit anyone from our Accounts Department into this
    section", or "admit people from South Africa, but nobody from
    Baphetikosweti".  Sioux provides a full log of client access
    allowing you to extract precise information about client
    demographics from your site.

  - CGI extensions for SSL support

    Sioux allows the writers of complex interactive sites to extract
    information from the client certificates which are presented during
    client authentication.

  - Python inside!

    Every copy of Sioux includes a dynamically linked Python
    interpreter, which means that siouxCGI scripts execute extremely
    quickly. This makes Sioux ideal for highly interactive web sites
    which depend upon access to databases and other rich information
    sources for many pages.

    We are currently focusing development on the SiouxCGI Collection,
    a set of siouxCGI scripts to harness the power of Sioux.  The
    Collection will simply drop into any Sioux installation and give
    you a host of plug-and-play CGI functionality.

  - easy installation and configuration

    Simply download and extract the archive, and run the Sioux Setup
    utility.  Sioux is running in five minutes flat.

Sioux is based on the well-tested Apache web server. Thawte Consulting
extends its thanks to the team which produced such a high-quality code
base and clean design for Apache.  Sioux also makes use of the
cryptographic library known as SSLeay for which we thank Eric Young and
Tim Hudson. Please see Sioux's copyright notice for details.

