It has been more than nine months since my last release, but it is finally
here.  Release 0.6 of my hfs_fs module is now available from my web page
and will be uploaded to Sunsite.  (see LSM entry for locations)

hfs_fs 0.6 is a loadable filesystem module for Linux kernels 1.3.67
and later.  It enables your Linux machine to mount Macintosh-formatted
media (floppies, SCSI hard disks, Zip disks, CDROMs, etc.).  This
release supports the file formats of the CAP and Netatalk file servers
with no additional patches.

This is the first release to support non-trivial writing to Mac disks.
While the implementation is not yet complete (notable omissions are
deletion of files/directories and truncation of files), it is sufficient
for transferring files between a Linux machine and a Mac when one or both
is not networked.  Work continues to implement the missing features.

This release requires gcc 2.7.0 or later.

