Hello all again :)
  and many greetings from Athens, Greece.

  Things seem to have gone quite well for Xaw3d-1.1 over the past
 little while (this past year, that is :)) since I only received one
 patch for it since the last release. Having converted to ELF for quite
 a while now, I thought I'd put out an updated Xaw3d-1.1, namely
 Xaw3d-1.1a. It has everything the old version had plus Heiko Schroeder's
 (heiko@pool.informatik.rwth-aachen.de) patch for SmeSB (many thanks for
 the fix Heiko :)) concerning bitmap positioning inside menu items (the
 bitmaps were not centered but positioned a few pixels below the center).
 The binary release includes both a.out and ELF libs (the a.out ones are
 the exact same ones with the 1.1 release - I didn't bother to recompile
 them with the above patch as a.out is becoming obsolete real fast). Also
 included are static libs compiled with the -g option (libXaw3d-g.a) so
 that one could get debugging info from the Xaw3d code as well.

  The new sources and binaries for Linux have been downloaded to sunsite,
 and are currently in /pub/Linux/Incoming (hopefully just for a little while).
 Their final location is in /pub/Linux/libs/X. The file names are

  Xaw3d-1.1a-src.tar.gz
  Xaw3d-1.1a-bin.tar.gz

 and contain the complete source and binary versions of the library
 respectively.

  My Xaw3d resources follow; insert in your .Xdefaults file and tailor
 to taste :)

