-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

The IMAP daemon with shadow support can be found at:
ftp://svpal.org/incoming/shadow/imapd-shadow.tar.gz.

Here's the README file.

Linux IMAP2 daemon for shadowed passwords

Included below are the following files:

log_std.c		File which needs to be patched for shadow support
			(found in pine3.91/imap/systype/c-client)
imapd.Makefile		Makefile which replaces pine3.91/imap/c-client
				
If you need to recompile, replace the two files, cd into the imap/ 
subdirectory, and type "make lnx".  This will save you time from having to 
compile the entire Pine v3.91 package.

imapd.elf		ELF 32-bit executable IMAP daemon

imapd.std		Standard IMAP daemon
			  (compiled for those not supporting ELF)

The IMAP daemon was extracted from the Pine v3.91 source code.  I've 
compiled the program for those who have and don't have ELF support.  
This patch has been tested under Linux v1.2.13 (Slackware v3.0 
distribution) and Linux v1.3.62.  

INSTALLATION

1. Copy the appropriate binary to /usr/sbin as "imapd".

	cp imapd.elf /usr/sbin/imapd

	OR:

	cp imapd.std /usr/sbin/imapd

2. Make sure your permissions are set correctly.  

	chmod +rx /usr/sbin/imapd

3. Add the following line to your /etc/services file:

imap2   143/tcp              
imap2   143/udp

4. Add the following line to your /etc/inetd.conf file:

imap2  stream   tcp     nowait  root  /usr/sbin/tcpd    /usr/sbin/imapd

5. Restart your inetd program.

6. To see if you've done everything correctly, verify by telnetting to 
   port 143:

* OK titan.gunn.palo-alto.ca.us IMAP2bis Service 7.8(92) at Sun, 7 Apr 
1996 10:53:37 +0000 (GMT)

Greetings go out to Clarence Bakken, Russel Mar, and Vaughan Pratt.
If you have any problems or questions, send e-mail to Roger Hu 
(rogerh@gunn.palo-alto.ca.us).



