This is version 13.1 of nn-tk, compared to the previous
version I did a Linux binary for it has much improved group
handling, much improved functioning over a slow line and
article reference threading. The last two items apply to
the curses version as well.

NN is a heavy duty newsreader and the TCL/TK
interace adds extra features inluding two different
group selection menus, MIME handling,  an internal
editor and a panel showing thread structure
The source can be compile to either nn or nn-tk.
The binary is ELF, compiled for both nn and nn-tk and
and is dynamically linked, it comes with TCL7.4/TK4.0
shared libraries.

The source and binary distributions are in Incoming on
sunsite.ucs.edu and pub/nn/contrib on ftp.uwa.edu.au.



